<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frösön</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frösön is an island in the lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/storsjon">Storsjön</a> in Jämtland, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, opposite the town of Östersund. Its name derives from the god Frey, and it was a pre-Christian cult centre and the meeting place of the Jamtamót, the assembly of the self-governing Jämtland farmers. It holds the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/froso-runestone">Frösö Runestone</a>, which records the region's conversion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/froson.jpg" alt="Frösön" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreaze · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fr%C3%B6s%C3%B6n.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
